University of Bergen, N-5000 Bergen, Norway. Non-standard abbreviations: LAH (Fig. 1) refers to reduction with LiA1H4. Carotenoids of a Gliding Organism Containing Bacterioehlorophylls 241 extend the preliminary investigation of Pierson and Castenholz (1971), a carotenoid analysis was performed on their organism. The results are presented and discussed herein. Materials and Methods The organism was referred to as F-2 by Pierson and Castenholz (1971) and the culture carries the designation J- 10-fl in the culture collection of Prof. R.W. Casten- holz. Axenic cultures were grown anaerobically at 47~ with 4000 lux of continuous incandescent light. Medium D (Castenholz, 1969) was used after modification by addition of 1 g/1 glycylglyeine and 2 g/1 powdered yeast extract. Cultures were harvested by centrifugation following 3--5 days of growth. Pigment extraction, saponification and total pigment estimation were done as reported previously (Halfen and Francis, 1971). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nECOLOGICAL GENOMICS OF FILAMENTOUS ANOXYGENIC PHOTOTROPHIC BACTERIA INHABITING GEOTHERMAL (https://studylib.net/doc/13462064/ecological-genomics-of-filamentous-anoxygenic-phototrophi...)\nciteturn42search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.5 years ago; Crawled: last month; Frozen samples were thawed and resuspended in 100 &micro;l Medium DH (Castenholz’s Medium D; Castenholz, 1969a), then\n    webs of these and similar communities.\n    APPENDICES\n    155\n    APPENDIX A\n    CHAPTER 2 APPENDIX\n    156\n    Enzymatic lysis and DNA extraction. Frozen samples were thawed and resuspended in 100 &micro;l Medium DH (Castenholz’s Medium D; Castenholz, 1969a), then\n    homogenized with sterile mini-pestle in 2 ml screw cap tubes. 900 l Medium DH was\n    added to the homogenized sample, then lysozyme (ICN Biomedicals, Irvine, CA) was\n    added at approximately 200 &micro;g ml−1 , and the mixture was incubated for 45 minutes at\n    3